  <!-- 8. Assemblages, Technical & Computational Blocks -->
  <paragraphs xml:id="para-blocks-assemblages-technical">
    <title>Assemblages, Technical Environments &amp; Code Blocks</title>
    <p>
      Beyond the six primary block groups, PreTeXt provides standalone assemblages, source code listings, tables, side-by-side layouts, and mathematical environments:
    </p>

    <p>
      <alert>Preview:</alert>
    </p>
    <assemblage xml:id="ass-quantum-foundations-demo">
      <title>Quantum Foundations Summary</title>
      <p>
        Key operational principles for quantum mechanical systems:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p><alert>State Space:</alert> Isolated physical states correspond to unit rays in a complex Hilbert space <m>\mathcal{H}</m>.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><alert>Observables:</alert> Measurable physical quantities correspond to self-adjoint Hermitian operators <m>A = A^\dagger</m>.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p><alert>Time Evolution:</alert> Unitary evolution governed by the Schrödinger equation <m>i\hbar \partial_t |\psi\rangle = \hat{H} |\psi\rangle</m>.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </assemblage>

    <program language="xml">
      <code>
        <![CDATA[
